Package: pve-wedge-watchdog
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: earlyoom
Suggests: pve-manager
Description: reboot a Proxmox VE host via kernel watchdog when it wedges
 pve-wedge-watchdog keeps petting a kernel watchdog device only while the
 host is healthy. Health is memory pressure (PSI) plus a local SSH banner
 probe, which exercises fork, exec and page-in. When the host wedges under
 memory pressure -- sshd and journald dead, ping still answering, MemAvailable
 never low enough for earlyoom -- it stops petting and the kernel reboots the
 machine, even if this daemon itself is stalled.
 .
 Ships in dry-run mode and disabled; see README.Debian before arming it.
 .
 contrib/ has a Proxmox hookscript that refuses to start a PCI-passthrough VM
 whose pinned memory would not fit in MemAvailable.
